  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Rights-Based Solutions for Vulnerable Migrants Through a Migrant Resource and Response Mechanism (MRRM) in the South of Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The risky and complex journeys undertaken by migrants, reaching Libya and beyond, expose them as well as host communities to multiple protection and health risks. Due to the continuous and prolonged instability public services are mostly unavailable, the health system is fragmented, ineffective and lacks the ability to respond to health needs of migrants and the Libyan population. The needs of these vulnerable migrants are rarely met due to additional barriers in access.The situation in the south of Libya is even more severe than the rest of the country. To address humanitarian needs in Libya and provide direct assistance, IOM established the Migrant Resource and Response Mechanism (MRRM) programme which brings together in one mechanism humanitarian aid and a wide range of services and needs based assistance to migrants and vulnerable host community members, living in distress in urban areas. Assistance includes primary health care services, MHPSS assistance, non-food items and hygiene kits, protection services and referral to various more specialized types of assistance. Simultaneously, IOM will disseminate information materials about the risks of irregular migration and will work toward increased acceptance of migrants by the local community through the implementation of a community engagement initiative.</narrative>
  </description>
